      "content": "Mega doses of Vitamin C will not effectively treat an established bacterial infection, and while generally safe for many, large doses can sometimes affect kidney function. Relying solely on Vitamin C to clear a UTI is ineffective and dangerous because it won't kill the bacteria causing the burning. The safest approach is to manage your symptoms with increased water intake and plan to speak with a professional as soon as possible for a proper diagnosis.",
